#: ../../upstream/docs/user/build-customization.rst:105
msgid "``$READTHEDOCS_OUTPUT/html/`` (required)"
msgstr "``$READTHEDOCS_OUTPUT/html/`` （必需）"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/build-customization.rst:106
msgid "``$READTHEDOCS_OUTPUT/htmlzip/``"
msgstr "``$READTHEDOCS_OUTPUT/htmlzip/``"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/build-customization.rst:107
msgid "``$READTHEDOCS_OUTPUT/pdf/``"
msgstr "``$READTHEDOCS_OUTPUT/pdf/``"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/build-customization.rst:108
msgid "``$READTHEDOCS_OUTPUT/epub/``"
msgstr "``$READTHEDOCS_OUTPUT/epub/``"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/build-customization.rst:112
msgid ""
"Remember to create the folders before adding content to them. You can ensure"
" that the output folder exists by adding the following command:"
msgstr "请在添加内容前先创建文件夹。可添加以下命令确保输出文件夹存在："

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/build-customization.rst:120
msgid "Search support"
msgstr "搜索支持"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/build-customization.rst:122
msgid ""
"Read the Docs will automatically index the content of all your HTML files, "
"respecting the :ref:`search <config-file/v2:search>` option."
msgstr "Read the Docs 将自动索引所有 HTML 文件的内容，遵循 :ref:`search <config-file/v2:search>` 选项。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/build-customization.rst:125
msgid ""
"You can access the search from the Read the Docs :term:`dashboard`, or by "
"using the :doc:`/server-side-search/api`."
msgstr "你可以从 Read the Docs :term:`dashboard` 访问搜索，或使用 :doc:`/server-side-search/api`。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/build-customization.rst:130
msgid ""
"In order for Read the Docs to index your HTML files correctly, they should "
"follow the conventions described at :doc:`rtd-dev:search-integration`."
msgstr "为使 Read the Docs 正确索引 HTML 文件，文件应遵循 :doc:`rtd-dev:search-integration` 所述约定。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/build-customization.rst:134
msgid "Alternative syntax"
msgstr "替代语法"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/build-customization.rst:136
msgid ""
"Alternatively, you can use the :ref:`config-file/v2:build.commands` key to "
"completely override the build process."
msgstr "或者，你可以使用 :ref:`config-file/v2:build.commands` 键完全覆盖构建过程。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/build-customization.rst:150
msgid "But we recommend using :ref:`config-file/v2:build.jobs` instead:"
msgstr "但我们建议改用 :ref:`config-file/v2:build.jobs`："

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/build-customization.rst:167
msgid ""
"``build.jobs`` offers the same functionality as ``build.commands``, but in a"
" more structured way that allows you to define different commands for each "
"format, while also supporting installing system dependencies via "
"``build.apt_packages``."
msgstr ""
"``build.jobs`` 提供与 ``build.commands`` 相同的功能，但以更结构化的方式，允许为每种格式定义不同命令，同时支持通过 "
"``build.apt_packages`` 安装系统依赖。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/build-customization.rst:172
msgid "Custom Git checkout commands (advanced)"
msgstr "自定义 Git 检出命令（高级）"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/build-customization.rst:174
msgid ""
"Read the Docs supports overriding the default :term:`checkout job <pre-"
"defined build jobs>` with a custom sequence of :program:`git` commands. This"
" is useful for advanced workflows like sparse checkouts or custom cloning "
"strategies."
msgstr ""
"Read the Docs 支持用自定义 :program:`git` 命令序列覆盖默认的 :term:`checkout job <pre-"
"defined build jobs>`。这对稀疏检出或自定义克隆策略等高级工作流很有用。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/build-customization.rst:178
msgid ""
"To enable this feature, go to your project's :menuselection:`Settings` and "
"update the :guilabel:`Git checkout command` field. Enter one command per "
"line."
msgstr ""
"启用此功能，请前往项目的 :menuselection:`Settings` 并更新 :guilabel:`Git checkout command` "
"字段。每行输入一条命令。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/build-customization.rst:184
msgid ""
"When you define custom Git checkout commands, Read the Docs will not run the"
" default Git clone or checkout. Your commands must perform the clone and "
"checkout of the desired revision."
msgstr "定义自定义 Git 检出命令后，Read the Docs 不会运行默认的 Git 克隆或检出。你的命令必须执行所需修订版的克隆和检出。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/build-customization.rst:189
msgid ""
"If you just want to run some extra commands after the default Git checkout, "
"like unshallowing the clone or fetching extra branches, you should use the "
"``build.jobs.post_checkout`` user-defined job instead."
msgstr "如果只想在默认 Git 检出后运行额外命令（如取消浅克隆或获取额外分支），应改用 ``build.jobs.post_checkout`` 用户定义任务。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/build-customization.rst:193
msgid ""
"In case you want to clone submodules, you can use the :ref:`config-"
"file/v2:submodules` config key for that."
msgstr "如需克隆子模块，可使用 :ref:`config-file/v2:submodules` 配置键。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/build-customization.rst:196
msgid ""
"Commands are executed in order, in the repository working directory. You can"
" use :doc:`pre-defined environment variables </reference/environment-"
"variables>` such as :envvar:`READTHEDOCS_GIT_CLONE_URL`, "
":envvar:`READTHEDOCS_GIT_IDENTIFIER`, and "
":envvar:`READTHEDOCS_REPOSITORY_PATH`."
msgstr ""
"命令按顺序在仓库工作目录中执行。可使用 :doc:`预定义环境变量 </reference/environment-variables>`，如 "
":envvar:`READTHEDOCS_GIT_CLONE_URL`、:envvar:`READTHEDOCS_GIT_IDENTIFIER` 和 "
":envvar:`READTHEDOCS_REPOSITORY_PATH`。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/build-customization.rst:201
msgid "Example of custom Git checkout commands"
msgstr "自定义 Git 检出命令示例"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/build-customization.rst:211
msgid ""
"This is an advanced feature. Incorrect commands can prevent builds from "
"checking out code or can expose sensitive files in your repository. If you "
"are unsure, use :doc:`build customization with build.jobs </build-"
"customization>` instead."
msgstr ""
"这是高级功能。错误的命令可能导致构建无法检出代码或泄露仓库中的敏感文件。如不确定，请改用 :doc:`build customization with "
"build.jobs </build-customization>`。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/build-customization.rst:216
msgid "Examples"
msgstr "示例"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/build-customization.rst:218
msgid ""
"We've included some common examples where using :ref:`config-"
"file/v2:build.jobs` will be useful. These examples may require some "
"adaptation for each projects' use case, we recommend you use them as a "
"starting point."
msgstr ""
"我们提供了一些使用 :ref:`config-file/v2:build.jobs` "
"有用的常见示例。这些示例可能需要针对各项目用例做些调整，建议作为起点参考。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/build-customization.rst:223
msgid "Unshallow git clone"
msgstr "取消浅克隆"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/build-customization.rst:225
msgid ""
"Read the Docs does not perform a full clone in the ``checkout`` job in order"
" to reduce network data and speed up the build process. Instead, it performs"
" a `shallow clone <https://git-scm.com/docs/shallow>`_ and only fetches the "
"branch or tag that you are building documentation for. Because of this, "
"extensions that depend on the full Git history will fail. To avoid this, "
"it's possible to unshallow the :program:`git clone`:"
msgstr ""
"Read the Docs 在 ``checkout`` 任务中不执行完整克隆，以减少网络数据并加快构建。而是执行 `shallow clone "
"<https://git-scm.com/docs/shallow>`_，仅获取正在构建文档的分支或标签。因此依赖完整 Git "
"历史的扩展会失败。为避免此问题，可取消浅 :program:`git clone`："

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/build-customization.rst:242
msgid ""
"If your build also relies on the contents of other branches, it may also be "
"necessary to re-configure git to fetch these:"
msgstr "如果构建还依赖其他分支的内容，可能还需重新配置 git 以获取这些分支："

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/build-customization.rst:260
msgid "Generate documentation from annotated sources with Doxygen"
msgstr "从带注解的源代码用 Doxygen 生成文档"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/build-customization.rst:262
msgid ""
"It's possible to run Doxygen as part of the build process to generate "
"documentation from annotated sources:"
msgstr "可在构建过程中运行 Doxygen 以从带注解的源代码生成文档："

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/build-customization.rst:280
msgid "Use MkDocs extensions with extra required steps"
msgstr "使用需要额外步骤的 MkDocs 扩展"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/build-customization.rst:282
msgid ""
"There are some MkDocs extensions that require specific commands to be run to"
" generate extra pages before performing the build. For example, `pydoc-"
"markdown <http://niklasrosenstein.github.io/pydoc-markdown/>`_"
msgstr ""
"有些 MkDocs 扩展需要在构建前运行特定命令生成额外页面。例如 `pydoc-markdown "
"<http://niklasrosenstein.github.io/pydoc-markdown/>`_"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/build-customization.rst:301
msgid "Avoid having a dirty Git index"
msgstr "避免 Git 索引变脏"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/build-customization.rst:303
msgid ""
"Read the Docs needs to modify some files before performing the build to be "
"able to integrate with some of its features. Because of this reason, it "
"could happen the Git index gets dirty (it will detect modified files). In "
"case this happens and the project is using any kind of extension that "
"generates a version based on Git metadata (like `setuptools_scm "
"<https://github.com/pypa/setuptools_scm/>`_), this could cause an invalid "
"version number to be generated. In that case, the Git index can be updated "
"to ignore the files that Read the Docs has modified."
msgstr ""
"Read the Docs 在构建前需修改某些文件以集成部分功能。因此 Git 索引可能变脏（检测到修改文件）。若项目使用基于 Git "
"元数据生成版本号的扩展（如 `setuptools_scm "
"<https://github.com/pypa/setuptools_scm/>`_），可能生成无效版本号。此时可更新 Git 索引忽略 Read "
"the Docs 修改的文件。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/build-customization.rst:323
msgid "Perform a check for broken links"
msgstr "检查断链"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/build-customization.rst:325
msgid ""
"Sphinx comes with a `linkcheck <https://www.sphinx-"
"doc.org/en/master/usage/builders/index.html#sphinx.builders.linkcheck.CheckExternalLinksBuilder>`_"
" builder that checks for broken external links included in the project's "
"documentation. This helps ensure that all external links are still valid and"
" readers aren't linked to non-existent pages."
msgstr ""
"Sphinx 自带 `linkcheck <https://www.sphinx-"
"doc.org/en/master/usage/builders/index.html#sphinx.builders.linkcheck.CheckExternalLinksBuilder>`_"
" 构建器，用于检查项目文档中的断外链。这有助于确保所有外部链接仍有效，读者不会被链接到不存在的页面。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/build-customization.rst:343
msgid "Support Git LFS (Large File Storage)"
msgstr "支持 Git LFS（大文件存储）"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/build-customization.rst:345
msgid ""
"In case the repository contains large files that are tracked with Git LFS, "
"there are some extra steps required to be able to download their content. "
"It's possible to use ``post_checkout`` user-defined job for this."
